    <article data-l="confidentialite">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="upd">Last updated: <span style="white-space:nowrap">November 24, 2026</span></p>
      <p>This policy explains what information HABYCORE LLC collects through this website, how it is used and what your rights are. We collect only the strict minimum.</p>
      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Information you provide</b> through the contact form: name, company, email address, subject and content of your message.</li>
        <li><b>Technical data</b> logged automatically by our hosting provider for security and proper operation of the website (IP address, browser type, date and time of access).</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>This information is used only to respond to your requests, manage our business relationships and keep the website secure.</p>
      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p><b>We do not sell your personal information or share it for targeted advertising.</b> It is disclosed only to our technical service providers (hosting, email), who are contractually bound to confidentiality, or where required by law.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>This website uses no advertising cookies, analytics tools or tracking pixels. Only cookies strictly necessary for its operation may be set. We honor Global Privacy Control signals. If an analytics tool is added, this page will be updated and your consent will be requested where required by law.</p>
      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>Messages received are kept for no more than 3 years after the last exchange, then deleted. Connections to the website are encrypted (HTTPS) and access to data is limited to authorized personnel.</p>
      <h2>Your rights: US residents</h2>
      <p>Depending on your state of residence (including California under the CCPA/CPRA, Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, Utah and Texas), you may request access to, correction of or deletion of your information, and opt out of its sale or sharing. HABYCORE LLC does not sell or share data for advertising. You will not be discriminated against for exercising these rights.</p>
      <h2>Your rights: EU and UK visitors</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR, processing is based on our legitimate interest in responding to your requests or on pre-contractual measures. You have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability, as well as the right to lodge a complaint with your data protection authority. As your data is processed in the United States, transfers are subject to appropriate safeguards.</p>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This website is intended for professionals. It is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their data (Children's Online Privacy Protection Act).</p>
      <h2>Exercising your rights</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:contact@habycore.com">contact@habycore.com</a>. We respond within 30 days (45 days where California law applies), after verifying your identity.</p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>Any change to this policy is published on this page with its update date.</p>
    </article>

